      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T11:55:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The option name `gerrit.allowCommentsWithoutPermissions` is self-contradicting, if you have this permission, \"withoutPermissions\" can\u0027t be true since you have this permission.\n\nI think if a repo is read-only __all__ write operations should be blocked. I guess if you really want the current behavior you could still configure it using fine grained permissions, why do we need a shortcut option for this current behavior ?",
