      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T11:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which projects wouldn\u0027t be bothered by being spammed?\n\nBtw, I find that Gerrit\u0027s definition of the \"read only\" state [1] is not explicit about comments and notedb in general. It explicitly says: no new changes meaning no new submits -\u003e no source code changes. The fact that noteDb is stored in the same repository may be considered an implementation detail and may not conflict with the read-only state of a project. Anyway, in the past when we used database instead of Git based noteDb that would be the case.\n\nSo, what do we consider read-only? I don\u0027t see a problem with being able to comment on a (closed) change in a read-only project (assuming you are allowed to comment in general).\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/Documentation/config-project-config.html#project-section",
